        "translation": "An altruistic tendency is regarded as moral because it continually leads us to care about others, even more than we care about ourselves. Because we are always attentive to others, we quickly notice their suffering, pain, hardship, or illness and look for ways to help. Sometimes we help with no more than a word, a glass of water, or a pill; at other times, it may be a large sum of money to help someone through a difficult period.",
