        "translation": "The conscious mind knows its own inner life. When we think about something, we still know that we are thinking about it. When we love or hate someone, we know that we are loving or hating. Alongside the mind’s busy activities, a quiet knowing continues to observe them. It is because the conscious mind can stand apart from thoughts and feelings that we can gradually practice bringing wandering thoughts to a stop.",
