        "translation": "With loving-kindness, we are also more confident when correcting a fellow practitioner. Because we have loved them and treated them well in daily life, they understand, when advice is needed, that we want to help them improve rather than criticize or blame. They also know that our goodness is not reserved for them alone: we treat everyone well. They are therefore more willing to accept what we say.",
