        "translation": "First, practicing a meditation method differs from the preceding parts of the path, which cultivate conduct of body, speech, and mind. At Right Mindfulness, disciples of the Buddha must begin a definite meditation practice with determination. Without knowing how to sit in meditation, we have not cultivated the seventh step of the Noble Eightfold Path. Because it is the seventh step, all preceding stages are important foundations. Yet cultivating only the first six without proceeding to Right Mindfulness does not fulfill Buddhist practice completely.",
